<item>
            <title>[ITEP-87215] MLOps Integration Geti/DLS-PS/SceneScape</title>
                <link>https://jira.devtools.intel.com/browse/ITEP-87215</link>
                <project id="99912" key="ITEP">EdgeSW</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;&#160;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Feature request raised by Nokia &lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/open-edge-platform/scenescape/issues/782&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;[link]&lt;/a&gt; (copied here):&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&#160;__&#160;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Make DLStreamer, Intel Geti, and Intel Scenescape work together automatically, so a user doesn&#8217;t have to manually move videos, create projects, or handle models by hand.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&#160;__&#160;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&lt;em&gt;Video streams (RTSP / camera feeds) are:&lt;/em&gt;&lt;br/&gt;
&lt;em&gt;Captured once and reused for both training (Geti) and inference (DLStreamer)&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&lt;em&gt;Geti projects (datasets, labels, training configs) are:&lt;/em&gt;&lt;br/&gt;
&lt;em&gt;Created automatically via API, possibly based on a template (e.g., &#8220;person detection&#8221;)&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&lt;em&gt;After training:&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&lt;em&gt;Geti exports an optimized OpenVINO model&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&lt;em&gt;The model is automatically:&lt;/em&gt;&lt;br/&gt;
&lt;em&gt;Downloaded&lt;/em&gt;&lt;br/&gt;
&lt;em&gt;Stored&lt;/em&gt;&lt;br/&gt;
&lt;em&gt;Versioned&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;


&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;No manual model conversion or copying&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&#160;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;*****&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;This feature may be approached in phases, with careful planning and design to support various use cases. Initial use cases include:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&#160;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ol&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;Scene and cameras are configured first, no existing dataset or models (quick start path)
	&lt;ol&gt;
		&lt;li&gt;Geti host/IP and API token are configurable for SceneScape&lt;/li&gt;
		&lt;li&gt;Scene map and cameras are created, with video free-running (no detections)&lt;/li&gt;
		&lt;li&gt;User triggers a &#8220;Capture Video for Training&#8221; method, likely from the SceneScape UI&lt;/li&gt;
		&lt;li&gt;The system captures data as controlled by the user (e.g. using a start/stop toggle) from the scene management interface&lt;/li&gt;
		&lt;li&gt;All scene cameras are recorded to create a synchronized dataset suitable for both training and synchronized playback in SceneScape (initially, no option to record single cameras)&lt;/li&gt;
		&lt;li&gt;System prompts the user for the new Geti project name, creates the project (using sensible defaults), and transfers the recorded videos automatically&lt;/li&gt;
		&lt;li&gt;Geti project is automatically associated with the scene&lt;/li&gt;
		&lt;li&gt;After training, the user must trigger an update of the model (this does not happen automatically), including selecting the optimized model variant (e.g. FP16, INT8) from the SceneScape UI&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;/ol&gt;
	&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;Geti project already exists and needs to be associated with DLS-PS pipelines used by SceneScape
	&lt;ol&gt;
		&lt;li&gt;User can easily browse and select from available models (both local and remote) from within the SceneScape UI (e.g. the camera/pipeline config page)&lt;/li&gt;
		&lt;li&gt;System automatically caches any selected models on the image pipeline system&lt;/li&gt;
		&lt;li&gt;User can capture new synchronized datasets for retraining as needed using &#8220;Capture Video for Training&#8221; method as needed&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;/ol&gt;
	&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;


&lt;p&gt;&#160;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Core requirements:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&#160;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ol&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;UX must minimize the number of clicks by the user and automate where possible&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;All association between a scene and a corresponding model can be on the SceneScape side (Geti does not know about the associations and ideally requires no modification to support this MLOps flow)&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;Consider associating the model with the scene rather than individual cameras (review UX and use case impact here: does it make sense to run different models on different cameras?) -&amp;gt; No. Model should be only associated with the specific camera configuration. Not the scene.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;All class labels are managed on the Geti side, with no hard-coding of class names and processing of those classes on the SceneScape side (SceneScape MOT will track all objects by class without modification or configuration)&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;A given model must be usable by any number of scenes and pipelines (one-to-many)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;


&lt;p&gt;The model ID and version must be included in both camera and scene metadata to facilitate traceability from source dataset through to the system output (hashes may be used for independent verification)&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&#160;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class=&apos;table-wrap&apos;&gt;
&lt;table class=&apos;confluenceTable&apos;&gt;&lt;tbody&gt;
